---
description: Draft content (WIP case studies, placeholders, DraftNotes, /dev/ pages) shows on dev and feature-branch previews only
globs: Code/src/pages/**, Code/src/components/case-studies/**, Code/src/components/case-study/DraftNote.astro, Code/src/lib/env.ts, Code/src/lib/deploy-stage.mjs, Code/astro.config.mjs
alwaysApply: false
---

Auto-attaches when editing pages, case studies, or the Astro config. Draft content
(a case study in progress, placeholder images, `DraftNote`s, sandbox and specimen
pages) renders on the dev server and on Vercel previews of feature branches only.
Never on staging, production, or a local `npm run build`.

- Gate draft content on `showDraftContent` from `Code/src/lib/env.ts`, never on
  `import.meta.env.DEV` alone (it is `false` on every Vercel deploy, previews included).
- Case study drafts go in `Code/src/components/case-studies/drafts/`.
- Specimen pages go in `Code/src/pages/dev/` as dynamic routes whose `getStaticPaths`
  returns `[]` unless `showDraftContent`. A static page there still ships.
- Merging drafts into `staging` is a warning; into `main` it is an error
  (`npm run draft:check`).
- Never weaken the draft check or the `/dev/` build guard in `Code/astro.config.mjs`.

Full guidance: `Agents/context/draft-content.md`.
